Rene Andre Bedonia Jocsing, for CMSC 131 at the University of the
Philippines Visayas: every other file in the repository or archive that
carries this LICENSE. That includes the Makefile, the fixtures, the
starters, the validators, the solutions carried forward, and the
documentation. The README of the repository lists its own files. An
archive lists nothing, because its contents are the manifest.


CHANGES MADE TO CARTER'S FILES

Every change is marked in place with a comment identifying it as an
addition, and every change is described in README.md.

    asm_io.inc  gained a block, active only when ELF_TYPE is defined, that
                remaps _asm_main to asm_main and declares a .note.GNU-stack
                section.

    asm_io.asm  gained the same .note.GNU-stack declaration, because it does
                not include asm_io.inc.

    asm_io.asm  gained an echo in read_int and read_char. When stdin is not a
                terminal, each one prints what it just read, since no terminal
                is there to echo the keystrokes. A redirected run then produces
                the same bytes as a typed one.

    asm_io.asm  read_int now sets its result to 0 before it calls scanf and
                reads the count scanf returns. On end of input, or on a word
                that is not a number, it returns 0 and prints no echo.
                Carter's version returned an unset stack slot in that case.


NONCOMMERCIAL

Use of this repository as course material is noncommercial use. Students may
read, copy, run, and adapt it for their coursework. Anyone redistributing it
or a modified version of it has to keep this license, keep the attribution
above, and say what they changed.
